WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:07.840
As we continue to follow the absolute tragedy&nbsp;
that is taking place in Texas with power outages,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:12.000
people without hot water, people&nbsp;
without heat, people struggling to get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.800
food. We talked yesterday about&nbsp;
Republican Texas Governor Ted Cruz&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:21.440
flying off to Cancun with his family to hit&nbsp;
the beach. That was Ted Cruz's approach.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:25.920
Beto O'Rourke, former Democratic Senate&nbsp;
candidate and presidential candidate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:34.160
decided instead to phone bank and call elderly&nbsp;
folks to see if they were OK. But he also is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:39.280
making some very appropriate and very harsh&nbsp;
comments about Texas leadership actually going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:45.600
as far to say that Texas is approaching a failed&nbsp;
state status better, O'Rourke said. First of all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:50.960
so much of this was avoidable. Going back to the&nbsp;
deregulation of our electric grid here in Texas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:56.240
which has actually created an incentive to not&nbsp;
weatherize or protect against these events better.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.240 --> 00:01:01.440
O'Rorke Absolutely right. As we've told you&nbsp;
before, in 2011, Texas had power outage issues.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:07.920
An extensive report was compiled saying do these&nbsp;
things to protect yourselves in the future. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:13.360
weren't done. And it happened again, absolute&nbsp;
negligence by Republican leaders in Texas.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:18.640
But then that's going further and saying&nbsp;
the energy capital of North America cannot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:25.520
provide enough energy to warm and power people's&nbsp;
homes. We are nearing a failed state in Texas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:30.240
and it has nothing to do with God or natural&nbsp;
disasters. It has everything to do with those&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:37.760
in positions of public trust who have failed us.&nbsp;
People have died in Texas and tens of thousands&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:43.360
